-The pramātṛ–pramāṇa–prameya comparison preserves subject-pole, means of knowing and known field. Mediation gives each pole its operative form. The instrument can be investigated as perception, memory, language, determination and coordination without turning the Subject into an item inside it. A technical local subject-function is a functional assignment; the assignment does not establish phenomenal luminosity.
+The pramātṛ–pramāṇa–prameya relation preserves knower, means and known within their whole rather than beginning with three independently complete things. [C10 — Mediation](C10-Mediation-Pramana.md) specifies the mode and warrant through which something becomes known; [C16 — Inner Instrument](C16-Antahkarana-Inner-Instrument.md) distinguishes determination, appropriation and coordination. Investigating these means does not make the Subject an item inside them. A technical local subject-function is a functional assignment; the assignment does not establish phenomenal luminosity.
+
+The complete [crossed-zero recognition](../../matheme/ql/crossed-zero-re-entry.md) makes this distinction operative: `0 → Ø → X → Ø/X → (0/Ø)/(1/X) → 1 ↺ 0/1`. The instrument’s self-identification is disclosed as medium, the medium’s discriminated world becomes available with it, and recognition holds their relation without replacing the instrument or claiming ownership of the whole. The special native slash-form is not ordinary division by zero; the sixfold and eight-determination accounts retain their own work within the same theorem.
