@@ -36,0 +37,12 @@ The opening language must remain more direct than “ground” and “mark” un
+### The whole relation and its practical disclosure
+
+**Pramātṛ is the knower, Subjective Immediacy; pramāṇa is the means, Objective Internality; prameya is the known, World. Life / Mind is their whole relation.** Mind in the strong idealist sense is Life; the psychic fact of experience is equally constitutive of the account. “Mind as objective internality” names the mediating, world-disclosing office of mind within this whole, not a reduction of Life/Mind to a collection of inspectable states. The whole is lived through the relation of knowing, means and known; external observation itself takes place through an internality. A particular ego, self-description or model is one determination within that relation, not the proprietor of its containing World.
+
